    "## 8. Covariance and Correlation\n",
    "\n",
    "So far, one variable at a time (**univariate**). Now we ask how two variables move\n",
    "together (**bivariate**). The building block is, for each point, the product\n",
    "\n",
    "$$(x_i - \\bar{x})(y_i - \\bar{y}).$$\n",
    "\n",
    "- Both above their averages, or both below -> the product is **positive**.\n",
    "- One above, one below -> the product is **negative**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Average those products and you get the **covariance**. Its *sign* tells you the\n",
    "direction of the relationship. Its *magnitude*, unfortunately, depends on the units\n",
    "(measure height in mm vs. m and the number changes)."
   ]
